<title>ITALY: Fiat sees Italy car orders up 35 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>Fiat sees Italy car orders up 35 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian carmaker Fiat Auto, part of the Fiat industrial group, saw Italian car orders up 35 to 40 percent year on year in January, a Fiat spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the orders were boosted mainly by a government incentive scheme to scrap old cars for new introduced at the start of the year.</p>
<p>In recent weeks Fiat Auto has said it expects to see an increase of 200,000 to 250,000 vehicle sales over the nine months in which the cash bonus scheme is in operation.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
